# Office inbox

The input channel of the **{{OFFICE}}** office. Anyone - a human, or a Claude Code session
opened in this repo - appends an entry here. The Coordinator reads it at the intake step of
every cycle and turns it into backlog items. Only the Coordinator edits an existing entry:
you append at the bottom and delete nothing. This file is a log.

## Entry format

```
## 2026-01-31 14:30 - short title
Status: new
Urgent: no

What I want: one sentence.
Why: what changes for the product or for one of its users.
Done when: the observable condition that closes the request.
```

`Status` is the Coordinator's to move: `new` -> `queued: <item ids or paths>` once the entry has
become work, `needs-info: <question>` when it is not specified enough (answer by appending a new
entry that cites this one, never by rewriting the old one), `closed` once the items it produced
are resolved.

`Urgent: yes` means "before anything else this cycle". It is not a way around the merge gate:
while deliveries are unmerged the cycle does not dispatch at all - your merge unblocks the
office, not your urgency.

An entry that asks for a non-reversible decision does not become a backlog item: it comes back
to you as a request for an ADR. The Coordinator does not invent architectural decisions.

